      "writtenOn": "2020-07-13T05:57:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Do we even need to tell which one is a baseboard and which one is a board?\n\nCan we automatically use the lowest directory name as a target? For example, fizz doesn\u0027t have a baseboard. So, make BOARD\u003dfizz builds from board/fizz. volteer has volteer as a variant. So, we\u0027ll have\n\n  board/volteer/volteer\n\nbut make BOARD\u003dvolteer will build from board/volteer/volteer using board/volteer as a parent.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 20,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 21,
        "endChar": 45
      },
      "revId": "4d3fea813ba2be5e7b898afa34bee2a115510169",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
